course: dictionary
lesson: 4709
title: Honour: respect, pride and keeping your word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Honour has several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one to use. It can mean great respect, as in «in honour of» someone. It can also mean feeling proud and glad, as in «It is an honour to meet you».
explain: Honour can also mean being honest and keeping your word. «On my honour» means "I promise this is true." A person of honour can always be trusted. As a verb, honour means to show respect or to keep a promise: «honour a promise».
explain: To work out the meaning, read the clues. «The festival honours the spirits of ancestors» shows respect for people from long ago. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Honour can be a noun or a verb: you can have honour, or you can honour someone.
fact: «Honour» means great respect, pride, or being honest and keeping your word.
fact: In US English, honour is spelled «honor».
fact: «Bon Odori» is a calm circle dance at Japan's summer Obon festival, and it honours the spirits of family members from long ago.
fact: An «honour roll» is a US list of good pupils.
exercise: «The festival honours the spirits of ancestors.» What does honours mean here? | Argues with | *Shows great respect to | Sings loudly about | Forgets about
exercise: «It is an honour to meet you.» What does honour mean here? | *Something that makes you proud and glad | A small fee to pay | A loud noise | A kind of dance
exercise: Ali says «I will honour my promise.» What does honour mean? | Forget the promise | Write the promise down | Break the promise | *Keep the promise
test: Ella says «On my honour, I did not take it.» What does on my honour mean? | I do not know | Dishonest, I cheated | I am proud of my hat | *I promise it is true, I am being honest
test: Which is the US spelling of honour? | hanour | honur | *honor | honoure
exam: «Chivalry was the code knights were meant to follow: be brave and loyal, and honour God.» What does honour mean here? | Shout at | *Show respect and faithfulness to | Be afraid of | Forget about
